title: "Geography of Skill Specialization and Complexity"
message: "If you use this dashboard, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Howell
    given-names: Anthony
    affiliation: "School of Public Affairs, Arizona State University"
    email: ajhowel5@asu.edu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4211-0190"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AntJam-Howell/skills-econ-geog-dashboard"
url: "https://skills-econ-geog.netlify.app/"
abstract: >-
  An open-access interactive dashboard for exploring a U.S. county-year panel
  of labor and skill demand derived from 433.6 million Lightcast (Burning
  Glass) job postings, 2010-2024. The dashboard is built on the Observable
  Framework and ships the county-year panel as a static CSV asset, parsed
  client-side with d3.csvParse (no backend, no WebAssembly). Five pages cover
  spatial visualization, ranked tables and trends, bivariate county
  comparisons, individual county profiles, and a usage guide.
keywords:
